# Patterns that must never appear on the public moca docs (rossoctl.dev/moca/*).
#
# Moca's sandbox service and harness are open source, for self-hosting. The
# public docs must not carry information about internal deployments of them:
# their names (SBX0, SBX1, ...), cohorts, or endpoints.
#
# The site's sync step (rossoctl/.github scripts/sync-docs.sh) checks every file
# it publishes from docs/ against these patterns, and skips the whole Moca
# section on any match, listing the files. specs/, notes/, plans/, archive/,
# demos/, adrs/ and REORG-PLAN.md are not published, so they are not checked.
#
# One extended regular expression (grep -E) per line; blank lines and lines
# starting with # are ignored. SBX[0-9] is also built into the site's check.
[Ss][Bb][Xx][0-9]
[Ii]nternal cohort
